IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je21-nouns`
IMPORT `je21-art02-making`
IMPORT `je21-art09-10-subordinate-powers`

-- je21-tests-art09-10-subordinate-powers: tests for Articles 9 and 10.
-- The expected values were written by hand from the text of Articles 9 and 10 and Article 2(1) and (3) before the module was run.

§ `Articles 9 and 10 -- tests`

§§ `Names for the readings and the outcomes (the first of each pair is the default)`

`L5 adopted` MEANS `made by the States means adopted by the States Assembly, as Article 2(1)(a) and 2(3)(a) put it, so it covers Laws, Regulations and Acts`
`L5 Law only` MEANS `made by the States means a Law only`
`L6 amendments only` MEANS `the limits bear on provision that amends other legislation, and incidental provision of any other kind is not limited by them`
`L6 literal` MEANS `the power in Article 9(5) is limited to amendments of the permitted kind, and authorises incidental provision of no other kind`
`authorised` MEANS `Article 9(5) authorises the provision`
`barred` MEANS `Article 9(6) bars the provision`
`displaced` MEANS `Article 9(5) does not apply because provision is made to the contrary`

--                                                                           form                                              HRL 2000  the enabling legislation
`a Law that is neither the 2000 Law nor the enabling Law` MEANS `Legislation to be amended` OF `a Law`,                                      FALSE,    FALSE
`the Human Rights (Jersey) Law 2000`                      MEANS `Legislation to be amended` OF `a Law`,                                      TRUE,     FALSE
`the Law that gives the power`                            MEANS `Legislation to be amended` OF `a Law`,                                      FALSE,    TRUE
`other Regulations`                                       MEANS `Legislation to be amended` OF `Regulations`,                                FALSE,    FALSE
`an Act of the States`                                    MEANS `Legislation to be amended` OF `an Act of the States that is Jersey legislation`, FALSE, FALSE
`an Order`                                                MEANS `Legislation to be amended` OF `an Order`,                                   FALSE,    FALSE
`another instrument`                                      MEANS `Legislation to be amended` OF `another instrument having legislative effect in Jersey`, FALSE, FALSE
`UK extended legislation`                                 MEANS `Legislation to be amended` OF `UK extended legislation`,                    FALSE,    FALSE

§§ `9(1) Exercised from time to time; repeal, amend or replace`

#ASSERT `Article 9(1): the power may be exercised from time to time and includes a power to repeal, amend or replace` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 9(1): the power may be exercised from time to time and includes a power to repeal, amend or replace` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 9(1): the power may be exercised from time to time and includes a power to repeal, amend or replace` FALSE FALSE

§§ `9(2) to 9(4) Variation, classes, partial repeal (made after 28 March 2003)`

-- The day before, the day itself, and the day after 28 March 2003.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 9(2): the power may apply generally or be limited, or make different provision for different cases, classes, conditions, exceptions or factors` (YMD 2003 3 27) TRUE FALSE BECAUSE "Article 9(2) is confined to legislation made after 28th March 2003, and the Law does not say what holds for legislation made on or before that day"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 9(2): the power may apply generally or be limited, or make different provision for different cases, classes, conditions, exceptions or factors` (YMD 2003 3 28) TRUE FALSE BECAUSE "Article 9(2) is confined to legislation made after 28th March 2003, and the Law does not say what holds for legislation made on or before that day"
#ASSERT `Article 9(2): the power may apply generally or be limited, or make different provision for different cases, classes, conditions, exceptions or factors` (YMD 2003 3 29) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 9(2): the power may apply generally or be limited, or make different provision for different cases, classes, conditions, exceptions or factors` (YMD 2021 9 28) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 9(2): the power may apply generally or be limited, or make different provision for different cases, classes, conditions, exceptions or factors` (YMD 2021 9 28) TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 9(2): the power may apply generally or be limited, or make different provision for different cases, classes, conditions, exceptions or factors` (YMD 2021 9 28) FALSE FALSE
-- 9(3): one case or many; none is not mentioned.
#ASSERT `Article 9(3): provision about that many cases is within the power in Article 9(2)` 1 (YMD 2010 1 1) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 9(3): provision about that many cases is within the power in Article 9(2)` 5 (YMD 2010 1 1) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 9(3): provision about that many cases is within the power in Article 9(2)` 0 (YMD 2010 1 1) TRUE FALSE BECAUSE "Article 9(3) speaks of one or more cases and says nothing of provision about no case"
#ASSERT NOT `Article 9(3): provision about that many cases is within the power in Article 9(2)` 1 (YMD 2010 1 1) TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 9(3): provision about that many cases is within the power in Article 9(2)` 1 (YMD 2003 3 28) TRUE FALSE BECAUSE "Article 9(2) is confined to legislation made after 28th March 2003, and the Law does not say what holds for legislation made on or before that day"
-- 9(4): the answer for 9(2).
#ASSERT `Article 9(4): a repeal may be brought into force in part` (YMD 2010 1 1) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 9(4): a repeal may be brought into force in part` (YMD 2010 1 1) TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 9(4): a repeal may be brought into force in part` (YMD 2003 3 28) TRUE FALSE BECAUSE "Article 9(2) is confined to legislation made after 28th March 2003, and the Law does not say what holds for legislation made on or before that day"

§§ `9(5) and 9(6) The incidental power and its limits`

-- The brief's question: can an Order of a Minister (not made by the States) use the incidental power to amend a Law (made by the States)?  No: 9(6)(b).
#ASSERT `Article 9(5) and (6): what the incidental power does for the provision` `an Order` `a Law that is neither the 2000 Law nor the enabling Law` TRUE FALSE `L5 adopted` `L6 amendments only` EQUALS `barred`
#ASSERT `Article 9(5) and (6): what the incidental power does for the provision` `an Order` `a Law that is neither the 2000 Law nor the enabling Law` TRUE FALSE `L5 Law only` `L6 amendments only` EQUALS `barred`
-- And an Order can use it to amend another Order, another instrument or UK extended legislation (none made by the States).
#ASSERT `Article 9(5) and (6): what the incidental power does for the provision` `an Order` `an Order` TRUE FALSE `L5 adopted` `L6 amendments only` EQUALS `authorised`
#ASSERT `Article 9(5) and (6): what the incidental power does for the provision` `an Order` `another instrument` TRUE FALSE `L5 adopted` `L6 amendments only` EQUALS `authorised`
#ASSERT `Article 9(5) and (6): what the incidental power does for the provision` `an Order` `UK extended legislation` TRUE FALSE `L5 adopted` `L6 amendments only` EQUALS `authorised`
-- It cannot amend Regulations or an Act (made by the States) on the default reading of L5; on the other reading Regulations and Acts are not made by the States, and it can.
#ASSERT `Article 9(5) and (6): what the incidental power does for the provision` `an Order` `other Regulations` TRUE FALSE `L5 adopted` `L6 amendments only` EQUALS `barred`
#ASSERT `Article 9(5) and (6): what the incidental power does for the provision` `an Order` `other Regulations` TRUE FALSE `L5 Law only` `L6 amendments only` EQUALS `authorised`
#ASSERT `Article 9(5) and (6): what the incidental power does for the provision` `an Order` `an Act of the States` TRUE FALSE `L5 adopted` `L6 amendments only` EQUALS `barred`
#ASSERT `Article 9(5) and (6): what the incidental power does for the provision` `an Order` `an Act of the States` TRUE FALSE `L5 Law only` `L6 amendments only` EQUALS `authorised`
-- A body's other instrument is in the same position as an Order.
#ASSERT `Article 9(5) and (6): what the incidental power does for the provision` `another instrument having legislative effect in Jersey` `a Law that is neither the 2000 Law nor the enabling Law` TRUE FALSE `L5 adopted` `L6 amendments only` EQUALS `barred`
#ASSERT `Article 9(5) and (6): what the incidental power does for the provision` `another instrument having legislative effect in Jersey` `an Order` TRUE FALSE `L5 adopted` `L6 amendments only` EQUALS `authorised`
-- Regulations: limited by 9(6)(a) only, on the default reading.
#ASSERT `Article 9(5) and (6): what the incidental power does for the provision` `Regulations` `a Law that is neither the 2000 Law nor the enabling Law` TRUE FALSE `L5 adopted` `L6 amendments only` EQUALS `authorised`
#ASSERT `Article 9(5) and (6): what the incidental power does for the provision` `Regulations` `the Human Rights (Jersey) Law 2000` TRUE FALSE `L5 adopted` `L6 amendments only` EQUALS `barred`
#ASSERT `Article 9(5) and (6): what the incidental power does for the provision` `Regulations` `the Law that gives the power` TRUE FALSE `L5 adopted` `L6 amendments only` EQUALS `barred`
#ASSERT `Article 9(5) and (6): what the incidental power does for the provision` `Regulations` `other Regulations` TRUE FALSE `L5 adopted` `L6 amendments only` EQUALS `authorised`
#ASSERT `Article 9(5) and (6): what the incidental power does for the provision` `Regulations` `an Order` TRUE FALSE `L5 adopted` `L6 amendments only` EQUALS `authorised`
#ASSERT `Article 9(5) and (6): what the incidental power does for the provision` `Triennial Regulations` `the Human Rights (Jersey) Law 2000` TRUE FALSE `L5 adopted` `L6 amendments only` EQUALS `barred`
#ASSERT `Article 9(5) and (6): what the incidental power does for the provision` `Triennial Regulations` `a Law that is neither the 2000 Law nor the enabling Law` TRUE FALSE `L5 adopted` `L6 amendments only` EQUALS `authorised`
-- On the other reading of L5 Regulations are not made by the States, so 9(6)(b) bars them from amending a Law as well.
#ASSERT `Article 9(5) and (6): what the incidental power does for the provision` `Regulations` `a Law that is neither the 2000 Law nor the enabling Law` TRUE FALSE `L5 Law only` `L6 amendments only` EQUALS `barred`
#ASSERT `Article 9(5) and (6): what the incidental power does for the provision` `Regulations` `an Order` TRUE FALSE `L5 Law only` `L6 amendments only` EQUALS `authorised`
-- An Act of the States is neither Regulations nor legislation not made by the States, on the default reading: neither limit bears on it.
#ASSERT `Article 9(5) and (6): what the incidental power does for the provision` `an Act of the States that is Jersey legislation` `a Law that is neither the 2000 Law nor the enabling Law` TRUE FALSE `L5 adopted` `L6 amendments only` EQUALS `authorised`
#ASSERT `Article 9(5) and (6): what the incidental power does for the provision` `an Act of the States that is Jersey legislation` `the Human Rights (Jersey) Law 2000` TRUE FALSE `L5 adopted` `L6 amendments only` EQUALS `authorised`
#ASSERT `Article 9(5) and (6): what the incidental power does for the provision` `an Act of the States that is Jersey legislation` `a Law that is neither the 2000 Law nor the enabling Law` TRUE FALSE `L5 Law only` `L6 amendments only` EQUALS `barred`
-- Provision made to the contrary: the model does not decide.
#ASSERT `Article 9(5) and (6): what the incidental power does for the provision` `an Order` `an Order` TRUE TRUE `L5 adopted` `L6 amendments only` EQUALS `displaced`
#ASSERT `Article 9(5) and (6): what the incidental power does for the provision` `an Order` `a Law that is neither the 2000 Law nor the enabling Law` TRUE TRUE `L5 adopted` `L6 amendments only` EQUALS `displaced`
#ASSERT `Article 9(5) and (6): what the incidental power does for the provision` `an Order` `an Order` FALSE TRUE `L5 adopted` `L6 literal` EQUALS `displaced`
-- Incidental provision that is not an amendment (a saving, say): L6 decides whether the limits reach it.
#ASSERT `Article 9(5) and (6): what the incidental power does for the provision` `an Order` `an Order` FALSE FALSE `L5 adopted` `L6 amendments only` EQUALS `authorised`
#ASSERT `Article 9(5) and (6): what the incidental power does for the provision` `Regulations` `the Human Rights (Jersey) Law 2000` FALSE FALSE `L5 adopted` `L6 amendments only` EQUALS `authorised`
#ASSERT `Article 9(5) and (6): what the incidental power does for the provision` `an Order` `an Order` FALSE FALSE `L5 adopted` `L6 literal` EQUALS `barred`
#ASSERT `Article 9(5) and (6): what the incidental power does for the provision` `Regulations` `a Law that is neither the 2000 Law nor the enabling Law` FALSE FALSE `L5 adopted` `L6 literal` EQUALS `barred`
-- A reading of L6 does not alter an amendment's answer.
#ASSERT `Article 9(5) and (6): what the incidental power does for the provision` `an Order` `a Law that is neither the 2000 Law nor the enabling Law` TRUE FALSE `L5 adopted` `L6 literal` EQUALS `barred`
#ASSERT `Article 9(5) and (6): what the incidental power does for the provision` `an Order` `an Order` TRUE FALSE `L5 adopted` `L6 literal` EQUALS `authorised`

§§ `9(7) Made under all the powers under which it may be made`

#ASSERT `Article 9(7): the subordinate legislation is treated as made in exercise of this power` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 9(7): the subordinate legislation is treated as made in exercise of this power` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 9(7): the subordinate legislation is treated as made in exercise of this power` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Article 9(7): the subordinate legislation is treated as made in exercise of this power` FALSE FALSE

§§ `10 Technical documents`

--                                                    legislation  free of charge  technical  aimed at a specialist
`a technical standard available free`  MEANS `Facts about a document` OF FALSE,       TRUE,           TRUE,      TRUE
`a technical standard sold for a fee`  MEANS `Facts about a document` OF FALSE,       FALSE,          TRUE,      TRUE
`legislation from another jurisdiction` MEANS `Facts about a document` OF TRUE,        TRUE,           TRUE,      TRUE
`a leaflet not about a technical product` MEANS `Facts about a document` OF FALSE,     TRUE,           FALSE,     TRUE
`a technical manual for the general reader` MEANS `Facts about a document` OF FALSE,   TRUE,           TRUE,      FALSE

#ASSERT `Article 10: the power to make subordinate legislation includes incorporating the document by reference` TRUE `a technical standard available free`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 10: the power to make subordinate legislation includes incorporating the document by reference` TRUE `a technical standard sold for a fee`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 10: the power to make subordinate legislation includes incorporating the document by reference` TRUE `legislation from another jurisdiction`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 10: the power to make subordinate legislation includes incorporating the document by reference` TRUE `a leaflet not about a technical product`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 10: the power to make subordinate legislation includes incorporating the document by reference` TRUE `a technical manual for the general reader`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 10: the power to make subordinate legislation includes incorporating the document by reference` FALSE `a technical standard available free` BECAUSE "Article 10 gives the States power to amend a Law to allow incorporation by reference and does not itself allow it, and no such amendment is given"
